binary-discrete-diffusion-sudoku demo — NOTICE

This directory (apps/binary-discrete-diffusion-sudoku/) is a CPU-only clear-
experiment toy inspired by:

  Casado Noguerales, von Rütte, Schölkopf, Hofmann, Raoufi,
  "Binary Discrete Diffusion: Candidate-Set Diffusion for Logic and Planning
  Tasks", arXiv:2610.28543 (2026)
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.28543
  Author page: https://rodcasnog.github.io/research/

Found via a bookmarked X post by @rodcasnog:
  https://x.com/rodcasnog/status/2113287405142675759

No official code repository was located as of 2026-10-28 (searched arXiv
abstract/HTML, the author's research page, and public GitHub queries). This
app is therefore an **independent minimal re-implementation** of the candidate-
set / binary-symmetric vs masked diffusion comparison on synthetic 9×9 Sudoku,
with a tiny (~150k-param) transformer — NOT a reproduction of the paper's 43M
DiT / Sudoku-Extreme numbers.

No warranty. Research / demo use. Trained weights stay out of git (work/ is
git-ignored).
